    <title>Regarding Henry</title>
    <desc>An unscrupulous corporate lawyer, Henry Turner (Harrison Ford) will do whatever it takes to win a case, and treats his family with the same degree of ruthlessness. After Henry gets caught in the middle of a robbery and is shot in the head, he wakes from a coma to find that he has amnesia and can't even remember how to do the simplest of tasks. As he recovers and relearns how to function, Henry reveals a much kinder and more thoughtful personality, much to the surprise of his family and friends.</desc>
    <language>en</language>
  </programme><programme channel="Super-Channel-Vault-CA" start="20260618080000 +0500" stop="20260618093500 +0500">
    <title>Harold and Maude</title>
    <desc>Cult classic pairs Cort as a dead-pan disillusioned 20-year-old obsessed with suicide and a lovable Gordon as a fun-loving 80-year-old eccentric. They meet at a funeral, and develop a taboo romantic relationship, in which they explore the tired theme of the meaning of life with a fresh perspective.</desc>
    <language>en</language>
  </programme><programme channel="Super-Channel-Vault-CA" start="20260618093500 +0500" stop="20260618115000 +0500">
    <title>Chinatown</title>
